<!--Post: 11254--><!--Time: 1110531570-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11254"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 11, 2005 - 12:59 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The symbol may have two meanings. It could symbolize his preference for female victims and a desire for those who wear eye glasses. It most probably provides an insight into Rader&#39;s violent sexual fantasies. It seems he derived gratification from binding, torturing and killing women who wore eye glasses.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11254-->
<!--Post: 11272--><!--Time: 1110549808-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11272"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 11, 2005 - 6:03 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I agree with all of you, hey do you think Rader&#39;s mother worn glasses, maybe that&#39;s where it started, I hear she was a good person but Rader being a sociopath one never knows. I think he was looking at Zodiac symbols when he made it, trying to put the three letters into one idea, but it didn&#39;t quite turn out right<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11272-->
<!--Post: 11287--><!--Time: 1110557127-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11287"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Freya<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Freya<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 11, 2005 - 8:05 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Bmodule, this was a while ago, but did you ever see the Saturday Night Live skit with Kirstie Alley &#40;during the Cheers years&#41; in which she played an alien whose eyes were in her breasts, and she was offended because everyone keep making &#34;eye&#34; contact with her? That&#39;s what his symbol reminded me of. Why do I mention this? Because the symbol seems incredibly adolescent for a killer who wanted to terrorize the public. Any ideas why? <BR>Wow, Ivyleaguer, I just read your post after completing my paragraph. I agree with your ideas. Do you think that the drawing seems more like the work of a juvenile, someone sexually undeveloped?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11287-->
<!--Post: 11351--><!--Time: 1110604631-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11351"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 11, 2005 - 9:17 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Glasses - somebody wake up skov!  If Ivy_leaguer thinks there might be a glasses connection, I&#39;m sold. <BR> <BR>I also agree with Rocky - it does look like a bass-ackwards treble hook.  There - now you&#39;ve done it.  Ruined all my afternoon fishin&#39; fantasies with that damn BTK. <BR> <BR>But you know what - those look like very angry eyes to me.  The &#34;evil-Bert&#34; mono-brow &#40;or rim, whatever&#41; gives them a nasty look.  Maybe a lot of people wouldn&#39;t find this symbol scary, but to me the thing looks like evil eyes over a spread-eagled, depersonalized, stick victim &#40;who, I admit, may or may not have a tail....it only goes so far and still makes BTK&#41;.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11351-->
<!--Post: 11355--><!--Time: 1110607489-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11355"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 11, 2005 - 10:04 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The B obviously looks like women&#39;s breasts. 1960&#39;s student nurse mass murderer Richard Speck eventually grew breasts as he served his life sentence in prison. How this was done I don&#39;t know or want to know but I think BTK was just planning ahead.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11355-->
<!--Post: 11367--><!--Time: 1110611638-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11367"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 11, 2005 - 11:13 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Eye glasses, in cinema, are used to make a woman appear naive, meek and innocent. &#40;Men too, see Clark Kent&#41; <BR> <BR>Richard Speck could have grown breasts, I believe, by stopping the production of testosterone in his body. If he was a sex offender it would be pretty easy to arrange to have that proceedure done medically, even in prison. <BR> <BR>I missed Kirsty Alley on SNL, which is too bad. I have always thought she had a nice pair of eyes.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11367-->
<!--Post: 11368--><!--Time: 1110611986-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11368"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 11, 2005 - 11:19 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Glasses can also render a superhero totally unrecognizable, maybe Denny took his glasses off during his crimes, which would explain why no one could recognize him as BTK. I may owe the PD an apology.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11368-->
<!--Post: 11373--><!--Time: 1110621655-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11373"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->J_eric<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->J_eric<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 12, 2005 - 2:00 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Makes me wonder just what else Kansas declares &#34;not fit to print&#34;?    <BR> <BR>Those curious about &#34;melding letters&#34; may well want to check out my thoughts on &#34;rh&#34; &#40;Cheryl Bates/Riverside Comm. College desktop poem&#41; at the ZodiacKiller site, as well as &#34;Z&#34; and the &#34;crosshairs&#34; of which many, many people have commented.  The concept is neither original nor particularly witty.   If anything, I wonder if Rader was copying Zodiac, assuming that Zodiac&#39;s messages made it into Kansas&#39;s errr... appropriate press....back in the late 60&#39;s and early 70&#39;s. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11373-->
<!--Post: 11416--><!--Time: 1110686546-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11416"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 12, 2005 - 8:02 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I believe the BTK Strangler chose female victims who wore eye glasses or embodied the qualities of innocence and naivete. The perpetrator felt he could control her and exact vengeance. Roy Hazelwood, a former criminal psychologist with the FBI argues serial murderers tend to select female victims who appear respectable, innocent and meek. They select them to destroy their innocence and demonstrate the victims were not as innocent as they appeared.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11416-->
<!--Post: 11418--><!--Time: 1110687256-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11418"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 12, 2005 - 8:14 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->One more thought on glasses, if you were btk, and thrived on instilling fear, wouldnt it cause more fear if your vic couldnt see you? maybe he took their glasses from them.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11418-->
<!--Post: 11424--><!--Time: 1110692769-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11424"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 12, 2005 - 9:46 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->zodiac wore glasses?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11424-->
<!--Post: 11436--><!--Time: 1110713562-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11436"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, March 13, 2005 - 3:32 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->This is gonna drift a little off-thread, but we have too many already to start another just for this. <BR> <BR>Talking about melding letters and it being juvenile reminded me of when I was in sixth grade. Me and some friends started forming a &#39;Man From U.N.C.L.E.&#39; club with the yellow I.D. badges and all. The whole thing evolved into a contest to see who could Smush the letters U-N-C-L-E into the coolest looking design. So I&#39;m assuming that 6th grade is about the normal age that boys experiment with letter melding &#40; not that I&#39;ve ever been all that normal but because everyone else did it too &#41;. <BR> <BR>Recalling how I had spent my sixth grade year reminded me that while troling the web for some fresh information I&#39;d read that Josephine Otero was known as the new girl in her sixth grade class, which in addition to putting that tragedy into a new, and yet even darker perspective, caused me to wonder what in the hell was going on in Rader&#39;s mind in 1974. But I did have a hunch. <BR> <BR>After checking the dates: <BR> <BR>Rader marries Paula in 1971, he&#39;s 26, she&#39;s 23; both at a relatively horny stage in life still. So then I check the Lutheran doctorine which does allow pretty free rein on birth control. So if they didn&#39;t want to have kids right away, didn&#39;t mean that they had to abstain from sex. <BR> <BR>But it seems a strange coincidence, that part of his secret, sexually motivated alter existence was a &#34;secret symbol&#34;, with boobies, reminiscent of normal sixth grade behavior, and that he had been married for three years &#40;without any kids&#41;. <BR> <BR>Then in 1974, at the scene of his first murder &#40;as far as we can document so far&#41; the one single thing that stands apart from all of the rest of the crime scene is the evidence of him molesting a sixth grade girl. His second attempt at a victim was 21 years old, but her picture looks like she was 16. Then in 1975 his first kid is born &#40;who would ,if full term, been conceived in late november of 1974. <BR> <BR>After that, the age of his victims progress in age and, at least from what we know as fact right now, Rader has not molested, or killed, another child since the Otero&#39;s. <BR> <BR>The question being, and I AM ACTUALLY ASKING A QUESTION, because I&#39;m not psychologically inclined, Could his motive been to psyche himself up to the task of siring offspring. <BR> <BR>Of course its obvious that the killings were for sexual gratification and he kept doing it because he wanted to, but would he have been able to get his wife pregnant without using the first two murders as either a way of, how you say, steeling his resolve, or even fantasizing about them to...um...get his setter to stand at point?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
