<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11719"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 17, 2005 - 12:31 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->....speaking of beta.... <BR> <BR>I just noticed that his symbol, with the back of the B separated &#40;presumably to accent the boobs&#41; makes it look like a lowercase Greek omega sitting on top of a half-hearted Japanese &#34;hon&#34; &#40;Êú¨&#41;, which is half of the symbol for Japan &#40;Ni-hon: Êó•Êú¨&#41;, and which is in fact derived from the very T-K-ish symbol for tree &#40;ki: Êú®&#41;. [Note: the Japanese characters will hopefully show up if you set Unicode encoding in your browser.] <BR> <BR>Do I think that his signature contains hints for Greece and Japan, two of his pit-stops in the Air Force?  Not really.  I agree with Linnieskid that it&#39;s probably just a doodle for BTK with boobs and/or glasses &#40;eyes&#41; in it.  HOWEVER, if bodies or &#34;hot&#34; cold-cases turn up in those overseas locales, I might be revising that opinion.  I know several of you are actively looking in those directions, and I would encourage it.  Perhaps there is a web-sleuth board in Japan, his longest stay overseas &#40;2 years near Tokyo&#41;.  I know Verm_inve is looking for Japan cold cases.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
