<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11865"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 19, 2005 - 11:17 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Pax56, I&#39;m awake and ready to report for duty so here goes. <BR> <BR>The year of the sheep symbol is very close and it is Zodiac. <BR>Btk was into the Zodiac and likely looked into the Zodiac&#39;s symbol and communications to find inspiration for his own symbol. <BR> <BR>&#34;She went to slaughter like a lamb.&#34; <BR>From &#39;The Confession&#39; sent anonomously to the Riverside, California Enterprise newspaper on November 19, 1966 describing the murder of Cheri Jo Bates. <BR> <BR>The murder and communication is long believed by many to be the earlist known murder and communication from a killer who would late become known in the San Fransico Bay area as The Zodiac. <BR>BTK being a regular church going man liked the lamb reference and looked for the zodiac symbol for the year of the lamb and found that in the Chinese zodiac there is no year of the lamb but rather the year of the sheep. When he saw the symbol he turned it side ways and saw a TK in it. He added the B to it and there he had his symbol. <BR>He was not a good shepherd, he was an evil shepherd. <BR> He would watch over the lambs and then lead them to slaughter. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
