<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11958"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Brown_tornado<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Brown_tornado<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, March 21, 2005 - 4:10 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hey Ya&#39;ll &#40;that&#39;s Kansaspeak&#41;, <BR> <BR>Do you remember the &#34;flash&#34; that the police &#40;LaMunyon days&#41; and KAKE used to try to talk to BTK? It was a pair of upside down eyeglasses, right? I think that may have something to do with the secret symbol. Whaddya think? It sure has similarities. And if this isn&#39;t a link between the &#40;victims-glasses&#41; and the symbol, than what the hell is it? What did the eyeglasses mean?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11958-->
<!--Post: 11965--><!--Time: 1111456193-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11965"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, March 21, 2005 - 5:49 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->BTK had some facination with eyeglasses but I am not sure what the connection was. <BR> He wore them and so did his victims. He left Nancy Fox&#39;s glasses upside down on her dresser. He took Marine Hedge&#39;s glasses with him. He discribed where in the Otero house that Josephine&#39;s glasses were. <BR>Maybe he was familiar with another murderer who felt he was superior to others and could get away with a perfect crime. Back in 1920&#39;s Chicago, Nathan Leopold and Richard Leob killed Bobby Franks in a thrill kill just to get away with a perfect murder. It wasn&#39;t. Leopold left his glasses at the crime scene. A very common frame and a very common prescription except for one thing, the hinges were of a special patent. Only three had been sold in Chicago. One to a woman, one to a respected attorney and one to Leopold.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11965-->
<!--Post: 11969--><!--Time: 1111462260-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11969"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, March 21, 2005 - 7:31 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->If, the BTK Strangler remained silent during the last year he would still enjoy freedom. His desire for recognition as a successful serial murderer and decision to resume communication with the media and the Wichita Police Department resulted in his apprehension last month. The inability to remain silent undermined his freedom. <BR> <BR>It seems the eyeglasses symbolized a sexual fetish and his preference for murdering women who wore them. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11969-->
<!--Post: 11972--><!--Time: 1111469112-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11972"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, March 21, 2005 - 9:25 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Yes, Brown, I think you&#39;re right.  I think that we can backtrack the glasses &#34;flash&#34; as proof that we are not the first to interpret the &#34;eyes/breasts&#34; part of the symbol as glasses.  Earlier, we were all wondering about the glasses in the &#34;flash&#34;, and were thinking that the fact that the police seemed to be keying on glasses was mostly &#40;if not entirely&#41; due to BTK&#39;s sketch of the glasses on the dresser.  Otherwise, it would have been based on the thread of glasses running through the victims.  That seemed like something of a stretch for the police - a bit &#34;out of the box&#34;, and rather atypical for WPD. <BR> <BR>I think they needed another &#34;2&#34; to make &#34;2&#43;2&#34; on glasses, and the secret symbol was it.  I believe that the suggestive interpretation as breasts is one of Rader&#39;s intended &#34;readings&#34; of the symbol, but the deeper reading is eyes or glasses - looking over the zodiac symbol for year of the lamb &#40;sheep&#41;.  The combination of the glasses and the lamb character give a complete reading to the symbol, just like a good kanji projects its meaning as a function of its parts &#40;and the parts, in turn, their parts&#41;. <BR> <BR>If I were to read that symbol as a kanji character in a sentence, it might have either of two meanings - one for BTK &#40;&#34;watching over&#34; - like a wolf&#41; and one for his victims &#40;&#34;glasses victim&#34; - like a lamb&#41;. <BR> <BR>I&#39;m betting that skov, Johno, and IL are right about his fascination/fetish with glasses.  If so, Rader&#39;s recordings of his crimes and his unreleased communications may indicate the role of glasses more explicitly.  There may also be something embedded in one or both of the puzzles that we have missed.  It seems to be rather important to him.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11972-->
