</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, April 02, 2005 - 9:41 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->From Skov via TransAtlantic Relay Network and Ricochette Service: <BR> <BR>I found this symbol from the movie  &#34;The Blair Witch Project&#34; and it realy get close to BTK¥s symbol if you  add the B part. This might be significant. <BR>I¥ll keep reserching trying to find out how the people behind the film choose/ put together that symbol for their film. <BR><a href="http://www.macdesktops.com/images/1600x1200/ACBlairWitch1600x1200.gif" target=_top>http://www.macdesktops.com/images/1600x1200/ACBlai rWitch1600x1200.gif</a> link to the TBWP <BR> <BR> <BR>Here is a link to the movie: <BR><a href="http://www.blairwitch.com/" target=_top>http://www.blairwitch.com/</a> <BR>  <BR>Could you please post this on the thred &#34;symbol&#34; for me on the forum? it is under the head thred &#34;BTK Communications&#34; <BR>  <BR>  <BR>Hope life is good to you... <BR>  <BR>hugs...skov  <BR>  <BR> <BR>Note: Skov actually had the images set up side by side as an attachment but I couldn&#39; post it so this link is the same as the one in the first post &#40;for comparison&#41;.-bmodule <BR>            | <BR>            V <BR><a href="http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/news/11078330.htm" target=_top>http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/news/11078330.htm</a> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
