<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12586"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lostdog<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lostdog<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, April 02, 2005 - 7:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Regarding ìJapanese bondageî --  Check out the ìChrist on the Crossî thread. <BR> <BR>I posted some information regarding Shibari Kihbaku. <BR> <BR>I learned this morning that Josie Otero was hung with hemp rope. <BR> <BR>Hemp rope is the media of choice in traditional Shibari. <BR> <BR>I started that ì Christî thread with a ìpig in a pokeî post. <BR> <BR>It keeps getting thrown off topic&#40;s&#41;. <BR> <BR>I invite those who are mulling over Raderís tour in Japan and his evolution &#40;as it pertains to bondage&#41; to reinvigorate that thread. <BR> <BR>Christ was tortured and murdered in bondage. One cannot help but wonder about Raderís interpretation of Christís suffering as depicted in literature and sculpture and on canvass. <BR> <BR>_ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ <BR> <BR> <BR>I received my copy of ìNightmare in Wichitaî today and made it to page 60 at breakfast. <BR> <BR>Yes, I had toast and coffee while I read about the murder of Josie and her family. <BR> <BR>I donít really read ìtrue crimeî and I am cautious about the amount of violent images I permit myself to absorb. <BR> <BR>Yet, I buttered my bread while I read Beattieís hypothesis that Joseph Otero was forced to watch his young sonís death by suffocation. <BR> <BR>I began following this case as a way to mitigate my fears. <BR> <BR>If I was vigilant, the boogyman would have that much more difficulty in triumphing. <BR>If I had faith, if I nurtured a belief, if I channeled my energy with like-mindedÖ <BR> <BR>the BTK would be caught. <BR> <BR>What I did not count on was desensitization.   <BR> <BR>I read about the ex-cops who canít go fish or  go to sleep without BTK nightmares --  then I considered the ravages of my own BTK addiction. <BR> <BR>_ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ <BR> <BR>Back on topicÖ <BR> <BR>Chinese algbra? <BR> <BR>Mongolian Zodiac? <BR> <BR>The back of Paulís waistcoat on the Sergeant Pepperís album cover? <BR> <BR>WellÖ <BR> <BR>The symbol sure looks similar to something I drew on the inside flap of my Pee Chee folder in seventh grade when I started thinking about boobs a lot. <BR> <BR>Come to think of it... I still think about boobs a lot. <BR> <BR>Hereís the differenceÖ today, I can draw a picture of the boobs that catch my attention which look more like the attention catching boobs than the actual boobs themselvesÖ <BR> <BR>Wha? Wow, I think Tallulay was channeling me! <BR> <BR>Hey, Tbay donít give up on those ESL night classesÖ ohÖ  and donít forget to pick up a new 9 volt battery for your ouija board! <BR> <BR>Ö <BR> <BR>A slightly &#40;and uncharacteristically&#41; inebriated post from an empty bottle of Pinot that would put even the great LrryAnderson under the table as I debate with myself whether or  not to read page 61 orÖ just leave it. <BR> <BR>LsotGdo  <BR> <BR> <BR>P.S. Skov baby! I raised a glass for you. Skol! <BR> <BR>  <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
