<!--Post: 12621--><!--Time: 1112601735-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12621"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, April 04, 2005 - 1:02 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Somewhere in my madness today I thought something would be easy, so I started with BTK. &#34;Born To Kill&#34; sounds good. So starte looking through motorycle clubs, for symbols thatgo with BTK, Now it took me to Valkyrie or Valhalan or whatever and guess what. They have a run to stonehenge, Ancient text link them to after life, of all blond hair and blues eyes. and I am lead from there back to te motorcycle club. Oh yeah look hard enough you will come across a site by AmberSage, Not me, about this, and collecting slaves for the afterlife. Yeah B, the hemp,well good point.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12621-->
<!--Post: 12650--><!--Time: 1112678551-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12650"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, April 04, 2005 - 10:22 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->These Motorcycle dudes sound similar to the Arian Nation. Did you find any connection? <BR> <BR>Arian Brotherhood? <BR> <BR>I know its Arian something.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12650-->
<!--Post: 12659--><!--Time: 1112709527-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12659"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, April 05, 2005 - 6:58 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->B, I was told there is a club in cali, that is responsible for kidnapping and selling young girls, as soon as I get the link i will post it.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12659-->
<!--Post: 12779--><!--Time: 1113174140-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12779"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Flytodeb<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Flytodeb<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, April 10, 2005 - 4:02 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I don&#39;t think the BTK secret symbol is simple. If you rotate the pic, it just looks like BTK, but the way it is in the pic, the straight line &#40;the back of the B&#41; would symbolize the strangling in the throat area. The round part of the B would be the breast area, obviously. Then the four legs of the K would be the arms and legs of the female victim. The vertical line of the T would be inserted as torture. The BTK suspect had entirely too much time on his hands to come up with this secret signature. <BR>-Deb <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12779-->
<!--Post: 12786--><!--Time: 1113221105-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12786"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, April 11, 2005 - 5:05 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Fly, I agree. when dogface said &#34;my code name will be on the next victim&#34;, and Katheryn Bright was stabbed, and after seeing the secrect symbol, <BR>I think maybe he &#34;made&#34; Kathryn his symblol. <BR> <BR>Something around the neck, cut across under breasts, and 2 cuts for the legs of the &#34;k&#34;. <BR> <BR>Although he didnt have much time. <BR> <BR>LE did say 3 stab wounds, maybe thats how they were sure it was him.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12786-->
<!--Post: 12810--><!--Time: 1113281954-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12810"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, April 11, 2005 - 9:59 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I have an idea for the guys, since I don&#39;t want to see this stuff&#62; Can someone look up the bondage mags. from back in the 70&#39;s and see if his symbol is related in any way to that concept? Rader taught me a lot about codes. Becuase he wasn&#39;t as smart as Zodiac, he was only able to dycipher the z code so far. I got to that point the other day and figured out that part of the code. Rader made his symbols and codes from the parts of Z coded he could understand. So I agree that there is a lot more to the symbol then we see. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12810-->
<!--Post: 12814--><!--Time: 1113288070-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12814"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, April 11, 2005 - 11:41 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->What was that game: &#34;Hangman&#34; that we used to play by drawing a stick figure on a gallows as a way of scoring?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12814-->
<!--Post: 12859--><!--Time: 1113451243-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12859"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, April 13, 2005 - 9:00 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hey B, Remember the movie about this? The guy was a sniper and he would leave the hangman game with a word unfinished on the top of the building he was shooting from? When the cops finally caught up with him, he had these letters One for each victim to get to the end of the word. My point? LOL he left a symbol, anyone remember this movie?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12859-->
<!--Post: 12861--><!--Time: 1113457383-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12861"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, April 13, 2005 - 10:43 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I must have missed the movie, but I was thinking that there was a game like tic tac toe played on scrap paper called hangman and another played with a basketball where you had to make the same shot as the other player. If you missed you added a letter. I guess my memory aint what it used to be. I just remember drawing a gallows as a small child.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12861-->
<!--Post: 12880--><!--Time: 1113527835-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12880"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, April 14, 2005 - 6:17 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->B, <BR> <BR>The basketball game is called &#34;horse&#34; with many variations. B I was referring to the Hell&#39;s Angels in my post. They have a running relationship with the Arian Brotherhood which is the largest white supremist prison gang in exsistance. The Angels usually perform &#34;hits&#34; or provide &#34;crank&#34; to the &#34;AB&#34; as they are known in California. <BR> <BR>Em, <BR> <BR>I have a hunch that the motorcycle gang you are thinking of that kidnaps girls for prostitution are the Mongols. The Mongols are not large in numbers but they have a very hardcore membership of murders and rapist. The Mongols reputation is such that they went to war with the Hell&#39;s Angels and they won the right to wear their leather vests aka &#34;Colors&#34; with a bottom &#34;rocker&#34; aka panel with the word &#34;California&#34; on it. The Hell&#39;s Angels made it known that only Hell&#39;s Angels would be permitted to wear the word California on their colors. The Mongols challenged this &#34;rule&#34; and &#34;won&#34; the war after more than 15 yrs of murders and retaliation.  .  .   <BR> <BR>In Beattie&#39;s book he talks about a psychologist who suggested that WPD buy all the Bondage magazines and search for personal ads or pictures that might match a crime scene. If I remember correctly, WPD blew off this suggestion and never checked these publications.  .  .  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12880-->
<!--Post: 12980--><!--Time: 1113913025-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12980"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, April 19, 2005 - 5:17 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Yes we use to play &#34;Hang Man,&#34; as kids, tells you how old I am. I am sure Rader even though almost twenty something years older than me played it first. I am still thinking that the symbol has something to to with things that where going on around him, during the time before the Otero murder&#39;s. Either in bondage or in his case could be some idea he got out one his comic book collection. I believe Z had his need for numbers and that type of structual order. Where as Rader thought more along the lines of a writer. Even though he wasn&#39;t very self- creative and had to steal ideas from others. I feel the symbol is more artistic than the strict patterns that someone like Zodiac follows. So this symbol has sometime to do with the times we all have talked about IMO. But was a creative idea, instead of a functional idea. I hope that makes sense. Thanks Sheila<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12980-->
